<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p><m>A = {\{\text{the factors of 75}\}}</m></p><p>(a) List the elements of <m>A</m>.</p><p><fillin characters="25" name="ans1"/>  </p><p>(b) Find <m>n(A)</m>.</p><p><fillin characters="5" name="ans2"/>  </p></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>(a) Go through the candidates in order and test each one against the description. The factors of <m>75</m> come in pairs: <m>1 \times 75</m>, <m>3 \times 25</m>, <m>5 \times 15</m>.</p><p>So <m>A = {\{1, 3, 5, 15, 25, 75\}}</m>.</p><p>(b) Counting each element once, <m>n(A) = {6}</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>\left \{1 , 3 , 5 , 15 , 25 , 75 \right \}</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>6</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>